# Peruvian-Style White Beans

Based on [https://www.goya.com/en/recipes/peruvian-style-beans](https://www.goya.com/en/recipes/peruvian-style-beans) (wayback unavailable) and [https://www.thespruceeats.com/peruvian-beans-3029292](https://www.thespruceeats.com/peruvian-beans-3029292) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="5" image="peruvian_style_white_beans.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } or vegetable oil
- [ ] 1 medium [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [paprika]{ ing="paprika" } (smoked or sweet)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [ground turmeric]{ ing="ground-turmeric" } (for color)
- [ ] 2 cans (15 oz each) [white beans]{ ing="white-beans" } (cannellini or Great Northern), drained and rinsed (or 3.5 cups cooked beans)
- [ ] 1 cup [vegetable broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" } or water
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" } (or to taste)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }
- [ ] (Optional) 1 [ají amarillo pepper]{ ing="aj-amarillo-pepper" } or jalapeño, minced
- [ ] (Optional) 2 Tbsp fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] (Optional) [Juice of 1/2 lime]{ ing="lime-juice" }

## Recipe

1. Heat [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in a large skillet or saucepan over medium heat
1. Add [onion]{ ing="onion" } and cook until softened and translucent (5-7 min)
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }, and [turmeric]{ ing="ground-turmeric" }; cook until fragrant (~1 min)
1. Add optional ají amarillo or jalapeño if using
1. Add [beans]{ ing="white-beans" }, [broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [pepper]{ ing="aj-amarillo-pepper" }, and [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }. Stir to combine
1. Bring to a simmer, then reduce heat to medium-low. Cook uncovered, stirring occasionally, until liquid reduces and [beans]{ ing="white-beans" } are creamy (10-15 min). Lightly mash some beans against the side of the pan for a creamier texture
1. Remove [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }. Taste and adjust seasoning
1. Optionally stir in fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" } and [lime]{ ing="lime-juice" } juice before serving

## Notes

- Serve as a side dish, taco filling, over rice, or as a base for tacu tacu (Peruvian bean and rice patties)
- For tacu tacu: Mix cooked beans with cooked rice, form into patties, and pan-fry until crispy on both sides
- Ají amarillo is a Peruvian yellow pepper that adds authentic flavor but can be substituted with jalapeño
- Bean alternatives: Pinto beans or black beans work well with these seasonings and are widely available in US grocery stores
- For Instant Pot: Sauté onion and spices using sauté mode, add remaining ingredients, cook on high pressure for 5 minutes, then quick release
